  abstract = {INTRODUCTION: In this edition, Szymu\'s et al. conducted a systematic review revealing sexual dysfunction to be more prevalent in patients with Huntington's Disease compared to controls. CLINICAL REFLECTIONS: Sexual dysfunction in HD (SDHD) is common and significantly affects patient quality of life. Commonly used HD rating scales and treatment guidelines do not explicitly address SDHD, and research studies are limited by size and methodology. CLINICAL IMPLICATIONS: It is important that validated sexual dysfunction screening tools be utilised in clinical and research settings.},
